Subject: [PATCH] 1. Added Chain support DBUS property. 2. Added Certificate
 type DBUS property. 3. Added openssl command for certificate validation. 4.
 Certificate retrives/installation/deletion support added.

Service: xyz.openbmc_project.Certs.Manager.Server.Https
Object : /xyz/openbmc_project/certs/server/https/1
interface : xyz.openbmc_project.Certs.Certificate

Property : CertificateType
         xyz.openbmc_project.Certs.Certificate.Type.PEMchain   --- supporting
         xyz.openbmc_project.Certs.Certificate.Type.PEM        --- supporting
         xyz.openbmc_project.Certs.Certificate.Type.pkcs       --- not supporting

Property : ChainCertString
                           --- Will contain all chain certificate data.
Chain installing procedure:

To install Chain certificate first need to set certificate type to ChainPem to CertificateType Property then
busctl call xyz.openbmc_project.Certs.Manager.Server.Https /xyz/openbmc_project/certs/server/https/1 xyz.openbmc_project.Certs.Replace Replace s /home/root/cert.pem

PEM file should be contain private key otherwise error will come.

Single certificate can also support chain certificate but only first certificate it will take remaining certificate it will ignore.

Signed-off-by: Dillibabu <dillibabug@ami.com>
